Z||000000||fyerstarter||04-15-2001||07:34 PM||||Ok I finally got around to checkin the codes on my 87 GT, and I got a 32 (EGR) and a 35 (IAC). The symptoms are the car is idling very high 1400 RPM. I spent all day checking for vacuum leaks and everything looks good. I didn't take off the upper plenum and inspect the lines with a microscope but from what I can see there is no breaks and everything is plugged up the way it should be. There are no cracks (big enough to see) in the EGR tube. <P>From what I have read so far it could be either:<P>-Vacuum leak (pretty sure its not)<BR>-Bad IAC<BR>-Bad EGR Valve  or Solenoid<BR>-Bad PCV Valve<P>I'm off to check the PCV valve and the EGR but if anyone has any suggestions of procedures for troubleshooting this problem I would certainly appreciate it.<P>Thanks in advance<BR>||||reg||1
